      "data_quality_notes": "The report does not present a single explicit GROSS 'movement in prior year's provision' figure. The note explicitly states a NET surplus of GBP 7.2m relating to reassessment of prior years - this NET figure has been used as a fallback (hence prior_year_development_gbp_m is net). A gross claims development triangle is present in the claims development note, but the printed table in the source was partially parsed and reconstructing the gross PYD from the triangle was non-trivial; therefore the net figure was used. The gross premium mix entries were calculated by applying the percentages given in the segmental note to the division gross written premiums; an 'Other' residual line was added to balance to total. Rounding applied to three decimal places for amounts in millions. [RAG PYD NOT APPLIED: deterministic figure +17.300m has the opposite sign to both model values [-7.2, -7.2], which agree with each other; model values retained. Sign agreement between the models is not a reconciliation: where they differ in value the cohort and accrual scope of each still has to be settled from the filing (R140).]",
